  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Workplace compliance, social dialogue and OSH preventive culture promoted</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">C81- Labour Inspection Convention, which was ratified by T&#xfc;rkiye in 1951, guides the relevant national legislation. There are 947 labour inspectors, 223 of which are women (23,5%). Labour Inspection and Guidance services are provided through five hubs located in provinces of Ankara, Istanbul, Izmir, Bursa and Adana. 
Government has been putting efforts to involve social partners in ensuring compliance. Yet, guidance activities are conducted within the scope of proactive inspections. Hence, the Ministry needs to step up efforts to increase activities in a systematic and holistic manner beyond the scope of proactive inspections. ILO in collaboration with the MoLSS, Directorate General of Guidance and Inspection will implement an EU funded Project to address the needs of labour inspectorate. The Strategic Compliance Plan will be formulated and adopted, standard operating procedures will be improved, labour inspectorate will develop a roadmap for effective guidance. ILO will strengthen the capacities of the staff of municipalities and private sector to increase sectoral OSH knowledge and awareness among municipality officials, employers, employees to will contribute to a more effective and operable implementation of OSH legislation and policies in sectors and occupations more at risk.</narrative>
  </description>
